WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:10.019
Social and Emotional Learning, or SEL, has
moved to the center of the educational

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.700
landscape, and there's much to like about
this. But for SEL to be successful,

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.920
advocates need to ask some tough
questions. The biggest: "What the heck is

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:25.019
SEL, anyway?" Look, it's easy to build
momentum by letting SEL mean whatever

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:29.490
someone wants it to mean. But for it to
stick, proponents need to be clear about

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:35.130
what SEL is — to guard against the vendors,
ideologues, and snake oil peddlers who

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:40.140
will insist that SEL is whatever serves
their interests. I'd urge advocates to

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.450
take care that SEL emphasize its
implication for character and

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:49.829
preparation for responsible citizenship,
partly to allay concerns that SEL could

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:54.300
become a squishy distraction from
academics. I'm certainly not the

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.789
authority on what the definition of SEL
should be, but I can say that a lack of

00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:04.260
clarity will summon those eager to
promote their own agendas, and that's not

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:09.360
good for anyone — except the hucksters. 
How do you think schools should measure

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.220
Social and Emotional Learning? Let us
know in the comments. Also, let us know

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.299
what other topics you'd like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:24.140
sure to LIKE and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

